From 8553804b1a187547640f86ac8e28708eb07faae9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiniMax Code <minimax-code@local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:29:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: harden touch input lifecycle, analog composition and
 action ownership

Closes the XH-001 findings that were mechanical to fix:

- Player resolution is re-evaluated when the cached instance is gone, so a
  player that spawns after the HUD, or is replaced on respawn, is picked up
  automatically instead of silently disabling camera look.
- The analog curve is produced once, by the touch adapter. The InputMap
  deadzone no longer re-processes the adapter output, which compressed the
  low end of the joystick range.
- Touch cleanup releases only the actions the overlay owns, so a keyboard or
  gamepad holding the same action is never cancelled.
- NOTIFICATION_APPLICATION_PAUSED is handled alongside focus out, covering
  Android backgrounding.
- A hidden overlay no longer consumes touches or drives the player.
- The look delta uses the public apply_look_delta method instead of an
  untyped call to a private one.

Adds five headless suites (37 assertions) covering player lifecycle, analog
composition, keyboard coexistence, viewport resize and the real input path.
The existing integration suite now runs with the overlay visible; it
previously drove a hidden HUD, which is the state in which the hidden-overlay
defect hid.

12/12 suites and the 10-frame main-scene launch pass on Godot 4.7.2 headless.
Physical Android QA remains untested. HIGH-2 (fixed-pixel HUD, safe area) and
HIGH-3 (resolution-dependent look sensitivity) are deliberately deferred to
Claude's visual brief and a creator device decision.
